silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_02_twelve_leg_deep_dive_sections_06_unit_leg_concrete_anchor#unit_grams silm:hasLongDescription "The Unit_grams is Unit_grams: the SI gram unit node (symbol: g, dimension: mass, UCUM code: g); used as the unit-attribution source for WeightMeas_3450g; shared by any gram-valued measurement in the local olog. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'UnitNode', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
